# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRONTEND (Vite) — these are compiled into the public browser bundle.
# Only ever put values here that are safe to publish.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional. Read by src/app/data/adminPushSettings.ts. Web Push has no server
# component in this project, so the toggle stores a subscription that nothing
# currently delivers to.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER ONLY — Supabase Edge Function secrets.
#
# Set these with `supabase secrets set`, NEVER in this file, never in Netlify
# build variables, and never with a VITE_ prefix. Anything named VITE_* is
# inlined into dist/ and served publicly; an SMTP app password published that
# way hands over the whole mailbox.
#
#   supabase secrets set SMTP_HOST=... SMTP_USER=... SMTP_APP_PASSWORD=...
#
# Listed here for documentation only — the names, never the values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SMTP_HOST                  smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT                  465 (implicit TLS) or 587 (STARTTLS)
# SMTP_USER                  the sending Google account
# SMTP_APP_PASSWORD          Google App Password — full mailbox access, treat as a root credential
# SMTP_FROM_EMAIL            envelope sender; Gmail rewrites this unless it is a verified alias
# SMTP_FROM_NAME             display name and the brand name used in email headers
# ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL   fallback admin recipient; the authoritative value is
#                            email_dispatch_settings.admin_notification_email
# APP_URL                    https origin used to build links, e.g. https://example.com
# OUTBOX_DRAIN_SECRET        shared secret between pg_cron/pg_net and dispatch-emails
# MAIL_TRANSPORT             "google-smtp" (default) or "log" for a dry run
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected into deployed Edge
# Functions automatically. Do not add them to the frontend environment.
